      "message": "This probably trips the \"dangling rule check\" if you run `m checkbuild dist general-tests`.  Any file in out/* referenced as an input to a ninja rule must have a rule that writes the file to out/.  In this case, \"out/soong/module_bp_java_deps.json\" is read by the ninja rule to copy it to to dist/, but written by the Soong process and not by a ninja rule.  The usual solution for cases like this is to insert a dummy rule that does \"touch $(out)\" so ninja thinks it wrote the file.",
